==============================================================================
VERDICT
==============================================================================
  best fan-ON-vs-fan-OFF cepstral statistic anywhere : 4.42 sigma
  worst SAME-CONDITION null with the same detector    : 7.83 sigma
  best HPS statistic (K=3/K=5)                        : 4.27 / 3.57 sigma
  matching HPS same-condition nulls                   : 3.52 / 5.88 sigma
  candidate at 82.78 Hz: run a +4.42, run b +2.21 -> not repeatable

  NO BLADE COMB DETECTED. The test statistic never exceeds the measured
  same-condition false-alarm floor, and the best candidate does not repeat
  across two independent 60 s fan-ON captures.
  Method sensitivity (B5): a blade comb would have been found at >5 sigma
  if it carried >= -22 dB relative to the IF rms. It does not.

